{"term":"regard","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:85fa1b51cfb58d74a2","definition":"A steady look, a gaze.","example":"He bathed in the memory of her blondness, of her warm blue regard, and the sentiment permeated his sensibility with tenderness made the more rich because its object was someone long since dead.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["consideration","onlook","respect"],"antonyms":["neglect"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":["court of regard","disregard","in regard","in regard of","in regard to","irregardful","regardful","regard ring","with regard to","misregard"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regard#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:aa73110a8257c7c289","definition":"One's concern for another; esteem; relation, reference.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["consideration","onlook","respect"],"antonyms":["neglect"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["court of regard","disregard","in regard","in regard of","in regard to","irregardful","regardful","regard ring","with regard to","misregard"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regard#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0e7ed9cc57f7f63d97","definition":"A particular aspect or detail; respect, sense.","example":"This attempt will be made with every regard to the difficulty of the undertaking […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":["consideration","onlook","respect"],"antonyms":["neglect"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["court of regard","disregard","in regard","in regard of","in regard to","irregardful","regardful","regard ring","with regard to","misregard"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regard#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3fc7e4c47c39dfe7d0","definition":"The worth or estimation in which something or someone is held.","example":"Dolph. For the Dolphin,\nI stand here for him: what to him from England?\nExe. Scorne and defiance, sleight regard, contempt,\nAnd any thing that may not mis-become\nThe mightie Sender, doth he prize you at.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["esteem","repute"],"antonyms":["neglect"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["court of regard","disregard","in regard","in regard of","in regard to","irregardful","regardful","regard ring","with regard to","misregard"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regard#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9a26cb151fa2cda039","definition":"To look at; to observe.","example":"She regarded us warily.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["behold","clock","look","geek","kool","regard","squizz","take a butcher's","take a dekko","take a gander","vada","viddy","view"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["court of regard","disregard","in regard","in regard of","in regard to","irregardful","regardful","regard ring","with regard to","misregard","regardable","regarder","regardless","self-regard","self-regarding"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regard#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b69567ca7467260e2f","definition":"To consider, look upon (something) in a given way etc.","example":"I always regarded tabloid journalism as a social evil.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["esteem","hold","account","appraise","count","esteem","see","censure","consider","deem","hold","dub","find","interpret","judge","look upon","regard as","respect","think of","view as"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","